WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.442
In 1912, the Qing emperor announced his abdication.

00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:06.552
China's last emperor left the throne.

00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:10.622
The gates of the Forbidden City slowly closed in the morning light.

00:00:10.622 --> 00:00:12.860
Sun Yat-sen took office as provisional president.

00:00:13.698 --> 00:00:17.022
The Republic of China was formally established that year.

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:21.112
In the square, people waved and cheered, full of hope.

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:23.945
The republican system replaced the imperial system.

00:00:24.177 --> 00:00:26.810
People began talking about the nation's new future.

00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:30.208
However, the domestic political situation remained turbulent.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.060
Local forces were powerful, and opinions were not unified.

00:00:34.498 --> 00:00:37.152
The new government faced many difficult problems.

00:00:38.045 --> 00:00:40.445
The young republic did not move forward smoothly.

00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:43.856
Ordinary people hoped life would soon become stable.

00:00:44.506 --> 00:00:47.089
Children by the street curiously watched the new flag.

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:51.358
This year became a turning point in Chinese history.

00:00:51.358 --> 00:00:55.160
The era of imperial rule ended, and the republican era began.
